Two variants are useful: one that labels just a status, and one that labels a full order with details.

```typescript
// Exhaustiveness helper: compile error if a case is missed
function assertNever(value: never): never {
  throw new Error(`Unhandled status: ${JSON.stringify(value)}`);
}

// Label for a bare status
function statusLabel(status: OrderStatus): string {
  switch (status) {
