**Why `.bind(console)`?** Returning an unbound method can cause problems in some environments (older Node versions, certain browsers) where `console` methods rely on `this`. Binding makes the returned function safe to call on its own.

**Why the `never` check?** If you later add a level like `"trace"` to `LogLevel` without adding a case, TypeScript will raise a compile error. The `console.log` fallback also keeps things safe at runtime if an invalid value slips in from untyped code.

