## How it works

- **`TrafficLightState`** is a union of string literals, so invalid states are compile-time errors.
- **`transitions`** is a lookup table. `satisfies TransitionMap` guarantees that every state has an entry (add a new state and TypeScript will flag the missing transition), while `as const` preserves the literal types.
- **`NextState<S>`** derives the exact next state at the type level, so `nextState("green")` is typed as `"yellow"`, not just `TrafficLightState`.

