### Design notes

| Technique | Why |
|---|---|
| `as const` + tuple → union | Single source of truth for runtime values and compile-time types. |
| `satisfies` | Validates the table's shape while preserving literal types (unlike a plain `: Record<...>` annotation, which widens them). |
| Mapped type over the state union | Makes the transition table **exhaustive** — missing a state is a compile error. |
| Discriminated union for states | Allows each state to carry different payload; `state.phase` narrows correctly. |
| `assertNever` in `default` | Guarantees the compiler flags any unhandled new state. |
| `isTrafficLightState` type guard | Narrows `unknown` to the state union at runtime boundaries. |

